## 1712-1724 · 2026-10-04→05 · Base prompt pipeline diagram and model-level override investigation
No declarative model-level prompt override exists in opencode (closed schema). The only model-level path is the `experimental.chat.system.transform` plugin hook. The filler + global AGENTS.md approach remains the declarative workaround.

## 1725-1841 · 2026-10-05 · Refined global AGENTS.md prompt rules
I refined the global AGENTS.md (~/.config/opencode/AGENTS.md) through a series of prompt-rule additions: Tool Parallelism block (batch independent reads/writes, dependency is the only serialization reason, plan the call graph), "Answer questions in the text field, not in tool call prefixes," "Verify is a gate, not a step" (each step's output verified before next step begins; "No exception" is not verification), "Clean up after failure" (check for partial state — files, artifacts, processes; restore if resumable, clean up if not), and "Webfetch is for analysis, not downloading" (use webfetch when content is for reasoning in context; use a shell command for file downloads). The docs template was synced to match. AGENTS.md is the fast iteration surface (re-read per request), config is the slow surface (restart-gated). Negative instructions don't belong in positive rules; silence suffices when the model wouldn't do the wrong thing by default. The skill needs updating to prevent example-anchoring. Commits: e461ceb, 2a86420, f4843c3, eb657f7, b4d5632, 1870015, 5f0fae2, 3fbdb56.

