## 2227-2261 · 2026-10-05 · Designed 'Don't wait before, wait after' background-process monitoring rule for global AGENTS.md
Designed the "Don't wait before, wait after" rule for global AGENTS.md background-process monitoring. Key design constraints from iteration: (1) non-blocking process-existence check (not `wait`, not `ps | grep` pipeline), (2) sleep between checks not before the first, (3) one retry per command — do not loop (kills the `while` pattern that blocks the bash call), (4) capture output on terminal state in the same command. The `&amp;&amp;` vs `||` distinction was critical: `&amp;&amp;` sleeps when the process is alive, `||` would sleep when it's dead (backwards). Applied to `~/.config/opencode/AGENTS.md` "Using Your Tools" section.

## 2262-2299 · 2026-10-05 · Diagnosed MC ctx_reduce infinite loop: model stamps own reply, newest tags protected
Diagnosed the MC ctx_reduce infinite loop: the model stamps its own reply via `ctx_reduce`, but stamps don't remove (newest tags are protected from clearing), so context is unchanged → same reply next turn → stamps again → loop. Root cause in `magic-context-prompt.ts`: "stamping recent output is harmless" encourages stamping own reply; "Never stamp a user message" protects user messages only — no "never stamp your own reply" instruction. Finding saved to project memory (CONSTRAINTS #1144). I was the live reproduction of the bug in this same session.

