## 4217-4278 · 2026-10-07 · Tool-result 'empty message' misidentification: protocol-level root cause
Investigated the tool-result "empty user message" misidentification. Tried five prompt-rule approaches (classification, sequence, self-monitoring, temporal awareness, phantom-generation) — none worked. The user identified the root cause as a protocol-level bug: Anthropic-compatible API reuses tool_use IDs across separate calls, breaking pairing and causing the client to insert a phantom empty user message. Prompt rules cannot fix a protocol issue. Documented in `docs/research/tool-result-empty-message.md`.

## 4279-4285 · 2026-10-08 · Root cause of empty user message thinking blocks: Anthropic protocol
The "empty user message" thinking blocks are a protocol-level artifact: Anthropic's wire format puts tool results in `role: "user"` messages, so the model correctly reads a tool-result-only user message as an empty user turn. No prompt rule can fix this; the OpenAI protocol's dedicated `role: "tool"` avoids the issue entirely.

