The user asked about `create_schedule` as a shortcut (it inherits caller provider). I verified from source: `create_schedule` at L834 has `?? callerAgent.provider` fallback, but `create_agent` hard-requires provider. I checked whether they're equivalent — they're not. Schedule lacks `notifyOnFinish` (fire-and-forget), lacks subagent parent binding, and adds cron litter (create+run_once+cleanup vs one call). The inheritance is the good half of the schedule path; the right fix is upstream wiring it into `create_agent`, not routing delegation through cron.

