The decisive probe (calling `task` with a nonexistent agent type) printed the effective ruleset verbatim: `{"permission":"task","action":"deny","pattern":"*"}` — the correct wildcard shape IS present. Yet the tool remains advertised. So the removal filter at `request.ts:208-214` is not firing on our live line despite the correct rule. User updated opencode to 1.19.5; same behavior — stable across both versions.

