I tested whether a Paseo plugin could host the `task` override (collapsing to one plugin). Two independent blockers: (1) `defineAgentTool` / `tools` field on `agent.open.before` doesn't exist in installed 0.13.2 — docs describe 0.14-era SDK ahead of the release; (2) structurally, attachment only *adds* plugin-local tools — the hook surface has no channel to remove a provider built-in, so best case on any version is two competing `task` tools. Result negative but conclusive. Architecture stands as designed: two plugins.

