## 5046-5094 · 2026-10-29 · Hardened paseo-task spawn: workspace pin + daemon-list identity join
Continuing the paseo-task plugin spawn-mechanism arc. The prior review (glm) caught that `spawnDelegate` used top-level `agents.create({cwd})`, which could mint spurious workspaces when the parent agent's cwd didn't resolve to an existing workspace. I replaced that with `client.workspaces.ref(workspaceId).agents.create({...})` — no cwd-based placement in that path, so workspace creation is structurally impossible. Verified both directions against the live daemon: invalid parent → `Caller agent not found` with workspace count unchanged; success → child landed in my workspace with parent label, hook-applied `explore`, stripped title, inherited model. Also fixed two review-quality items glm's "tsc clean" had papered over: non-narrowing `assert.equal(result.ok, false)` patterns and missing strict config — tsc now genuinely clean with a committed `tsconfig.json` at `~/.config/opencode/tsconfig.json`, 32/32 tests.

U: from the disk record what's disk record? isn't rewriter knows which session it's running in?
The user's question hit the design point: the plugin knows its opencode session (`ToolContext.sessionID`), but `parent`/`workspaceId` are Paseo ids, and one opencode server process hosts many Paseo agents — so there's no "itself" in Paseo terms until you join the two. I probed the SDK's `agents.list()` payload empirically (types are hidden) and discovered it carries `runtimeInfo.sessionId` for every agent — the MCP wrapper just hides it. This replaced my disk-record scan (`~/.paseo/agents/&lt;workspace-slug&gt;/&lt;agentId&gt;.json`) entirely. The disk scan wasn't just inelegant, it was wrong in practice: on-disk `archivedAt` goes stale, and my own smoke tripped on it — a record that looked live produced `Caller agent not found`. The daemon list is by construction the view the daemon accepts, and it supplies `workspaceId` for the pin in the same call. Rewrote tests dropping disk-scan suites, rebuilt spawn harness around the list payload. Final: 29/29 tests (new `failList` redaction case), strict tsc clean, live smoke both branches. Spec + correction log committed (03929e4).

