## 5161-5190 · Completed task-as-paseo-plugin acceptance and shipped state
I ran the final live verification of the task override plugin, discovering the root cause of the repeated restart hangs: plugin init runs inside session creation — the server blocks awaiting the init promise, so any self-request from init (`client.app.agents()` or HTTP GET to its own `serverUrl`) never resolves. This was a structural impossibility in my "build-time list from live server" design; no unit test could have caught it because fakes answer. The fix: init registers with a static baseline list, background-refreshes `/agent?directory=` (5s bound), `execute` validates against the live list. A second latent bug surfaced in the same live repro: `ctx.serverUrl` is a URL object, not a string — the refresh was silently failing until I added a logged catch.

