#1363: Code must be committed to the local repo before being written to a rental box — writing directly to the box without a local commit risks losing work when the box is destroyed.
#1441: Rental-box billing discipline: a finished arc ends with the box destroyed in the SAME pass as the last measurement — do not present keep-or-destroy as an open question at arc end, and when the user signals the box should die, destroy immediately without liveness checks first. Unattended runs must leave zero billing instances active as the final state.
