#1443: In unattended qudata runs: if an instance disappears, treat the wallet as empty and wrap up immediately with a status report.
#1604: Never declare a chat-template or output-cleaning fix effective for reasoning leakage until its effect is confirmed on live responses; when emitting any reply, keep reasoning and tool-call internals out of the visible text stream entirely, including think or reasoning tag markers, because leaking that content into the response is the exact defect the template was supposed to eliminate and asserting it is fixed while it recurs is the correction.
#1665: A pointed-out gap, omission, or flaw in an artifact is NOT an edit command: present the proposed wording/diff and end the turn; edit and commit only after an explicit go. The user has corrected this "started editing without saying a word" pattern repeatedly (doc patches 2026-10-16/17, response-shape iterations); questions and observations are always answerable in chat first.
